3. WHAT THE DATA IS

AIDP-2K is synthetic. Every one of its 2,000 documents was generated by the code in
aidp-bench/corpus-gen/ from a published seed. Every person, address, account number, article and
amount in it is invented, and so is every company name, with two exceptions: one Portuguese
company is named after the publisher, Docupath, and the freight invoices print a vessel name that
carries a real shipping line's name, with real container-owner codes. Any other resemblance to a
real one is coincidence.

This repository contains no customer documents. The only figures in it that were derived from
real documents, processed on a commercially available IDP platform whose name is withheld, are the
AIDP-Field totals quoted in section 1 of the paper "Precision Beyond the Page", listed in
analysis/README.md: counts and shares taken over all accounts together, with no document, no
customer name and no value from any document.


4. MATERIAL FROM OTHERS

  - The software's dependencies are not part of this repository and keep their own licences:
    bwip-js (MIT), playwright (Apache-2.0) and mupdf (GNU AGPL-3.0-or-later). mupdf is needed only by
    three benchmark tools: the post-run diagnostics of aidp-bench/bench/post-run/, the page previews
    of aidp-bench/bench/corpus-sample.mjs and the optional second-reader lane of
    aidp-bench/bench/run-das.mjs. Regenerating the dataset and scoring results do not use it.
    Installing and using mupdf is subject to its own licence.
  - The public-benchmark audit (aidp-bench/studies/public-benchmark-audit/) quotes a few short values
    from the CORD dataset (Park et al., "CORD: A Consolidated Receipt Dataset for Post-OCR Parsing",
    2019, https://github.com/clovaai/cord), which is licensed CC BY 4.0. It contains no other text,
    image or annotation copied from the public datasets it studies: only its own counts and judgments,
    with pointers to each dataset's official files.
  - Product, company and dataset names belong to their owners.
